case cofc-cvar-tail-averse
uses cofc ^0.1.0
as_of 2026-09-28
summary "§1498(a) patent case in the CoFC, solved for the worst 10% tail (CVaR)."
notes "Ported from examples/cofc-cvar-tail-averse.json. A 28 U.S.C. § 1498(a) patent claim in the CoFC, at accrual: the claim is timely under § 2501 and nothing is pending elsewhere (§ 1500), so both are matter facts; being a § 1498(a) claim, it has no bid-protest track, no general-civil case type, and no non-patent branch (cited Forfeited events). The example's remove_edges listed the two barred fact edges; resolving those nodes through facts instead is what the engine's fact-unset warning asks for. Stakes scale the pack's own payoffs by `stakes`; the rate is illustrative."
perspective owner

parties {
  owner: applicant Corporation
  united-states: examiner Government
}

events {
  2026-09-14 Forfeited("e-filingfork-protest") by owner cite 28 U.S.C. § 1498(a)
  2026-09-14 Forfeited("e-casetype-general") by owner cite 28 U.S.C. § 1498(a)
  2026-09-14 Forfeited("e-patentfork-nonpatent") by owner cite 28 U.S.C. § 1498(a)
}

facts { limitations-check: e-limitations-timely, section-1500-check: e-1500-clear }
analysis { params: { rate: 850, stakes: 12 }, objective: { type: "cvar", alpha: 0.1 } }
